{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>For keeping.</b> For storage." "<b>For your generations.</b> In the days of Jeremiah; when Jeremiah would rebuke them — why are you not occupying yourselves with Torah? — they would say: Let us leave our work and occupy ourselves with Torah; how shall we be sustained? He brought out for them the jar of manna. He said to them: You — ״see the word of YHWH״ — it does not say 'hear' but 'see.' By this your forefathers were sustained. The Omnipresent has many agents to prepare food for those who fear Him."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:46.307230878Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}